BOSS FIGHT: ROUND ONE (15 seconds)

STYLE

Hyper-kinetic anime realism · neon-soaked cyberpunk alley · cinematic DOF · dynamic neon reflections · explosive impacts · dust and particle-rich atmosphere · realistic cloth and fluid simulation · glossy wet pavement · energy streaks and chromatic flares · hand-held camera shake with micro-jitter · high-contrast neon palettes · volumetric haze.

AUDIO

Deep servo torque · electric charge hum · visor boot-up whine · crackling arcs · shockwave booms · debris clatter · neon buzz · burning sparks · sliding metal · anime impact stingers · sub-bass rumbles · swirling wind turbulence from fast movement.

PHYSICS + FX

Impact Physics: Shockwaves push debris, dust, stickers, trash. Ground vibrates. Micro cracks and small craters form at impact points.
Air Dynamics: Wake turbulence around fast limbs; puddles ripple; rain bends around high-speed motion; heat distortion trails behind energy attacks.
Micro-Particles: Persistent neon grime, dust motes, drifting debris reacting to motion; time-slice moments freeze all particles perfectly.
Mech FX: Metal stress flex, vibrating armor plates, rotating eye rings, hydraulic steam jets, servo recoil kicks.
Energy FX: Concentric visor glyphs, beam-charge glow, arc sparks, afterimage streaks, light tunnels through dust clouds.
Destruction FX: Falling neon signs explode into shards, wall graffiti flakes blast off, trash bags burst with soft-body physics.
Environmental Light Reaction: Neon reflections ripple across wet ground; pink mech glow casts dynamic reflections; beam attacks illuminate dust clouds volumetrically.
Cloth & Body Physics: Jacket flapping, hood strings spring dynamics, strap lag, boots compress on landing, realistic anticipation and recoil.
Camera Physics: Handheld micro-shake on impacts, whip-pans, stabilization during slow-mo, rebound from shockwaves.
Time-Slice FX: Frozen debris, suspended droplets, static beam core flicker; camera moves independently during frozen moments.

CAMERA RULES

Always moving · expressive · hand-held · whip-pans · orbits · reverse dolly · vertical tracking arcs · proximity changes for scale · no static tripod shots.

SCENE TIMING (0.0–15.0s)
P0 — Anchor (0.0–0.3s)
Use the uploaded image as a dynamic opening frame. 
The mech’s armor plates twitch with micro-servo motion; tiny dust particles swirl; slight drift, rain haze, neon flicker.

P1 — Kinetic Visor Spin-Up (0.2–1.3s)

Camera WHIPS into a 360° micro-orbit around the kid, creating neon streaks across the lens.
The visor boots violently with spinning holographic polygons, targeting rings, and pulsing glyphs.
A shock ripple distorts the air: his jacket flares outward, debris lifts briefly in a gravity pulse, dust spirals into a corkscrew, puddles tremble.
Behind him, the mech’s giant face warps in fisheye smear from orbit speed.
Final sharp electric snap, camera snap-zooms into his glowing visor.

P2 — Mech Slam Shockwave (1.3–2.5s)

The mech SLAMS its hand into the ground.
Shockwave erupts: puddles explode outward, litter jumps, neon signs flicker violently.
Camera rattles with heavy micro-shake.

P3 — Slow-Mo Dodge (2.5–3.3s)

Kid leaps in stylized slow-mo; debris floats mid-air; rain curves around him with elegant air compression physics.

P4 — Drone Swarm Deploy (3.3–4.5s)

Backpack cracks open — micro-drones burst out, creating vortex spirals.
Camera spirals around the kid; neon reflections streak across metal and dust.

P5 — Mech Laser Charge (4.5–5.5s)

Extreme close-up of the mech’s glowing eye.
Rotating lenses, crackling charge buildup, heat distortion, neon signs glitch from the EM surge.

P6 — Reverse Dolly Sprint (5.5–6.7s)

Kid sprints forward.
Camera reverse-dollies at high speed; neon streaks, puddle sprays, straps and jacket flapping.

P7 — Beam Impact / Time Slice (6.7–7.4s)

Mech FIRES.
White-blue blast erupts.
World freezes in perfect time-slice: droplets suspended, debris frozen, sparks mid-flight.
Camera glides freely through the static explosion.

P8 — Aerial Strike (7.4–9.0s)

Kid rockets upward with air curling behind him.
He lands a glowing energy punch on the mech’s jaw—metal shards, sparks, shock ripples.

P9 — Dual Clash Recoil (9.0–11.2s)

Kid and mech strike simultaneously, triggering a massive shock-blast sphere that bends neon lights and hurls debris outward.
Camera performs a sideways high-speed dolly between them, skimming above the wet asphalt.
Sparks spray, trash tumbles past the lens, puddles erupt, reflections wobble like liquid glass.
Kid skids backward, flips into a perfect anime landing.
Mech smashes into the alley wall, shaking dust and debris loose.

P10 — Mech Wall Eruption (11.2–12.8s)

Buried in debris, the mech erupts outward, ripping metal sheets aside and blasting concrete chunks.
Low-angle upward camera push-in:
– puddles explode under its steps
– dust clouds billow
– neon tubes shatter in sparkling arcs
– pink mech glow lights swirling debris
The mech steps forward aggressively, eye blazing.

P10 — CHARGE-UP FACE-OFF (12.8–14.7s)

Camera pushes in fast toward both fighters, both actively powering up:
Kid’s fists crackle with rising electric arcs; visor glyphs spin; jacket whips violently.
Mech’s eye spins its lens rings; armor plates shake with energy buildup.
Dust, trash, and small debris rise into micro-levitation from the electromagnetic tension.
Neon signs strobe uncontrollably.
A floating pebble between them vibrates, then pops into dust from the power surge.

P12 — Cliffhanger (14.7 – 15.0s)
END on a sharp energy ignition ping, like the instant before Round Two.
